        "original_id": "8bd45040-2802-55b3-be70-5e43ef7807d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: San Antonio International Airport, Yakutat Airport, San Antonio, Texas, Yakutat, Alaska\n- Companies: M7 Aerospace\n- Codes: IATA SAT, ICAO KSAT, FAA LID SAT, IATA YAK, ICAO PAYA, FAA LID YAK\n- Topics: airport locations, airport service areas, airport ownership\n\nFacts:\n- San Antonio International Airport has IATA code SAT, ICAO code KSAT, and FAA LID SAT.\n- San Antonio International Airport is an international airport in San Antonio, Texas, and it serves the Greater San Antonio metropolitan area.\n- Yakutat Airport has IATA code YAK, ICAO code PAYA, and FAA LID YAK.\n- Yakutat Airport is a state-owned public-use airport located three nautical miles southeast of the central business district of Yakutat, Alaska.\n- Yakutat is a city and borough in Alaska with no road access to the outside world.\n- M7 Aerospace LP is an aerospace company headquartered on the property of San Antonio International Airport in Uptown San Antonio, Texas.",
